    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0536" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119 Military Clauses/1: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Germany (Sackett)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-08-17T17:00:00-04:00">August 17, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. The United Press despatch from Berlin reports that Germany and France are on
                    the point of initiating direct negotiations concerning the limitations placed on
                    German armaments by the Treaty of Versailles.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d286-f1"/>
                    The first conversations, according to this report, are expected to begin some
                    time next week upon the return to Berlin of the French Ambassador.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d286-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Do you have any information which would confirm this story?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
